<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piauí</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piauí is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, with its capital at Teresina, and the only north-eastern state whose capital lies inland. It was settled from the late seventeenth century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> ranchers moving from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a> and Pernambuco, and became a captaincy dependent on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a>. Its Serra da Capivara National Park contains thousands of prehistoric rock paintings and is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piaui.jpg" alt="Piauí" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E2m, Giro720 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_do_Piau%C3%AD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
